        <type>XStatus</type>
        <definition>XStatus XPmPlDevice_InitStart</definition>
        <argsstring>(XPm_PlDevice *PlDevice, const u32 *Args, u32 NumArgs)</argsstring>
        <name>XPmPlDevice_InitStart</name>
        <param>
          <type>XPm_PlDevice *</type>
          <declname>PlDevice</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const u32 *</type>
          <declname>Args</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>u32</type>
          <declname>NumArgs</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Start Node initialization for PlDevice. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>PlDevice</parametername>
<parametername>:</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>PlDevice pointer </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Args</parametername>
<parametername>:</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Arguments for PlDevice </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>NumArgs</parametername>
<parametername>:</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of arguments for PlDevice</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if successful else XST_FAILURE or error code</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Arguments consist of Power Domain Node Ids that PlDevice depends on </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Set the desired power domain dependency bitmask WfPowerBitMask is cleared and then set based on the arguments present in Args[]<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>NOC Power Domain : BitMask [0]</para></listitem><listitem><para>PL Power Domain : BitMask [1]</para></listitem><listitem><para>AIE Power Domain : BitMask [2]</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>Power Management for PLD device elements:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Power Domain Dependency management based on WfPowerBitMask<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Parent power-up events for domains (if parent exists)</para></listitem><listitem><para>Self power-up events for domains</para></listitem><listitem><para>UseCount Management</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>PL Init Start indicates that a new RM or static image has been re/loaded. We must get rid of any existing child nodes if at all there are any, since new topology can be formed with those</para>        </inbodydescription>
